              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Promotions lift volume a lot, but most do not pay back. They give away margin on units that would have sold anyway, and the post-promo dip takes back part of the extra volume."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "Each dot is one promotion. Above the dashed line it earned money; below it, it lost."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": ""
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "The pattern: a promotion pays off only when the product has margin to give away. Retail (black) sits at low margins and mostly below zero; Online (yellow) reaches the highest margins, where most promotions pay off."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        }
